he energy of z_δ has been identified by strong rooted convergence and occupation control. All choices remain finite.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-positive-rooted-clipping"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","kind":"claim","label":"Positive-temperature rooted output and clipping","locator":"07-positive-temperature.tex:680–737; eq:classical-eams-vector, eq:clipped-classical-vector","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-positive","statement":"For each fixed finite discretization, apply the smooth strong-limit lemma to the EAMS recursion to obtain a rooted z_δ with the scalar law Z_δ and rooted energy equal to its corrected edge sum. Since |m(T,X_T)|≤1, the scalar coupling yields ‖z_δ−clip(z_δ)‖≤C√δ, and root-shift continuity controls the energy loss. β₀, T and then δ are chosen to make the clipped rooted output arbitrarily near P_*.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","id":"field:572622cb04e8d2219e61fc315bf07d8c8a61f0fbf3d910ea9e41bb98d3103f4f","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.positive_input"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.classical_positive","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_positive%22%2C%22circuit.positive_rooted_clipping%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430